piles.length <= h <= 1e9","1 <= piles[i] <= 1e9"],"hints":["If speed k works, any faster speed also works. That monotonic \"works / doesn't work\" shape is a cue for binary search on the answer.","For a given k, the hours needed are the sum of ceil(piles[i] / k). Binary-search k between 1 and max(piles).","Compute ceil as (p + k − 1) / k and keep the hour total in a long. Find the smallest k with hours ≤ h."],"explain":"At speed 4 the piles take 1, 2, 2 and 3 hours (each pile rounds up), 8 hours in total, which fits `h = 8`. At speed 3 they take 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10 hours, too many. So the slowest speed that works is 4."},
