,7,5,2]","5"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[1000000,1000000,1000000,362781]","972877"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[1,10,5,1,10,1,1,1,8,9]","10"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[411297]","3"],"out":"137099","g":1},{"in":["[6,6,6,10,6,10,10,10]","1000000"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[1000000,1,1000000,371413,230601,626218,598537]","7"],"out":"1000000","g":1},{"in":["[749914]","1"],"out":"749914","g":1},{"in":["[10,1,5,3,7,2,4]","14"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[7,10,10,7,7]","1000000"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[208643,40833,801775,681277,975414,416910,112845,837203,489423,219065,580232,56285]","33"],"out":"208455","g":1},{"in":["[587256]","6"],"out":"97876","g":1},{"in":["[71093,465162,545649]","4"],"out":"465162","g":1},{"in":["[2,8,10,7,2,7,9]","1000000"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[6,8,10,1,2,10,1,1,9,10,7,1,10,8,5,1,1,10,1,7]","20"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[577441,382385,718710,753270,831164,528173,599677,930340,1]","1000000"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#6:892e4dc90a3c59dd\"","perf":{"label":"n = 50,000","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.ints(50000, 1, 1000000); int a1 = 60000;"},"refMs":16}],"lesson":"binary-search-on-answer","statement":"Choose a positive integer divisor `d`. Divide every value of `nums` by `d`, rounding each result up, and add them together.\n\nReturn the smallest `d` for which that sum is at most `threshold`. An answer always exists.","constraints":["1 <= nums.length <= 5e4","1 <= nums[i] <= 1e6","nums.length <= threshold <= 1e6"],"hints":["A larger divisor never increases the sum. So the condition \"sum ≤ threshold\" flips from false to true exactly once as d grows.","Binary-search d between 1 and max(nums), computing the rounded-up sum for each candidate.","Look for the smallest d that satisfies the condition: when it holds, set hi = mid; otherwise lo = mid + 1."],"explain":"Dividing by 5 and rounding up gives 1, 1, 1 and 2, which sum to 5 ≤ 6. Dividing by 4 gives 1, 1, 2 and 3, summing to 7, which is over the threshold. So the smallest divisor that works is 