","g":1},{"in":["[987421087,1,568823531,775548006,179714107,240374852,313946736,444433319]","2"],"out":"987421086","g":1},{"in":["[8,18,17,40,34,20,24,32,10,16,9,25,21,15,27,37,3]","2"],"out":"37","g":1},{"in":["[16,33,31,6]","4"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[24,20]","2"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[23,16,1,36,9,8]","6"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[24,40,13,11,22,17,10,14,30,33]","10"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[20,1]","2"],"out":"19","g":1},{"in":["[1,40,24,10]","2"],"out":"39","g":1},{"in":["[1,104503587,132176016,191966708,337317583,654612376,714383740,736343400,827048686,955081980,973803152,1000000000]","7"],"out":"87463121","g":1},{"in":["[40,35,34,29,22,11,8,5,1]","2"],"out":"39","g":1},{"in":["[40,22,37,31]","4"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[710998592,174207850]","2"],"out":"536790742","g":1},{"in":["[37,1,13,40,11]","2"],"out":"39","g":1},{"in":["[1,989425025,843319051,331206997,1000000000,131108878,784975922,533712223,676250693]","2"],"out":"999999999","g":1},{"in":["[1000000000,872248643,606207750,316117620,286859348]","5"],"out":"29258272","g":1},{"in":["[1,665403478,932396445,143516354,302965501,853519081,813050153]","7"],"out":"40468928","g":1},{"in":["[554824051,900755512,605364222]","2"],"out":"345931461","g":1},{"in":["[1000000000,692256109,96904513,221487243,232807861,543384074,660458290,864782243,511545983,556272378,581900416,859074220,1,862437219,205750766]","15"],"out":"2345024","g":1},{"in":["[226610780,1000000000]","2"],"out":"773389220","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#6:10037bc5b8139af5\"","perf":{"label":"100,000 baskets","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.distinct(100000, 1, 1000000000); int a1 = 1000;"},"refMs":11}],"lesson":"binary-search-on-answer","statement":"There are baskets at the distinct positions in `position`. Place `m` balls into baskets, at most one ball per basket, so that the smallest distance between any two balls is as large as possible.\n\nReturn that largest possible minimum distance.","constraints":["n == position.length","2 <= n <= 1e5","1 <= position[i] <= 1e9","The positions are distinct","2 <= m <= n"],"hints":["Sort the positions. Then ask: can I place m balls so every two are at least d apart?","Check d greedily: put a ball in the first basket, then in the next basket at least d further, and so on. Count how many fit.","If m balls fit for d, they also fit for any smaller d. Binary-search the largest d that works."],"explain":"Placing the 3 balls at positions 1, 4 and 7 makes the closest pair 3 apart. A minimum gap of 4 is impossible: after 1 the next free position at least 4 away is 7, and nothing fits after it. So the largest possible minimum force is 3."},
